  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose using a binary comb function heuristic to minimize the overlap integral C\u2085. The key idea is to create a structured pattern of non-overlapping pulses spaced symmetrically to avoid high overlaps at any shift. This approach leverages the symmetry and periodicity of the problem, aiming to create a near-optimal function with low maximum overlap. We adjust pulse count and spacing to balance overlap reduction against feasibility.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nDefine h: [0,2] \u2192 {0,1} with \u222bh(x)dx =1. Let h consist of m non-overlapping pulses, each of width w =1/m, spaced by s =1/(m-1). The function is periodic with period p = m(w +s). The overlap integral C\u2085 is computed as max_k \u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+k))dx, considering all shift directions.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Set m=5 based on computational experiments balancing overlap reduction.\nb) Initialize h as binary with 5 pulses: [0,0.2), [0.25,0.45), [0.5,0.7), [0.75,0.95), [1.0,1.2).\nc) Ensure \u222bh=1 by adjusting widths and spacings.\nd) Compute overlap integral using numpy.correlate.\ne) Refine m and s via heuristic search to minimize C\u2085.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nStart with m=5, w=0.2, s=0.25. Evaluate C\u2085 via cross-correlation. Consider m=4 or 6 if initial results are suboptimal. Ensure h remains binary and respects constraints.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nUses numpy operations efficiently. With n_points=100, computations are lightweight, completing within 600s.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nEnsure h is binary, \u222bh=1, and dimensions match. Re-evaluate C\u2085 using task metric.",
